{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PpuTQTCLKtTYvZaqm8WUP8","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (498KB). Full output saved to: C:\\Users\\Jyue\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-Jyue-Documents-1-projects-Software-Projects-pelangi-website\\da0fa83d-ba02-4da7-93da-79913d071b9e\\tool-results\\bwhjllwmg.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n## Codebase Patterns\r\n\r\n- Pages use `<Header />` + `<Footer />` from `@/components/`, wrapped in `<main className=\"min-h-screen bg-stone-50\">`\r\n- Content sections use `pt-28 pb-16 container-custom` for top-padding that clears the fixed header\r\n- `font-display` maps to Playfair Display (serif); `font-sans` maps to Inter\r\n- Tailwind custom colors: `stone-*`, `amber-*`, `primary-*`, `accent-*`, `sand-*`\r\n- Data files live in `site/src/data/` and export typed interfaces + arrays\r\n- Next.js App Router with `generateMetadata` for SEO; `metadataBase` set in layout.tsx\r\n- `@tailwindcss/typography` installed (iteration 1) — use `prose prose-stone prose-lg` for HTML content rendering\r\n- No ESLint config in project — skip `npm run lint`; use `npx tsc --noEmit` as the quality check\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Ralph Progress Log - Fri, Mar 13, 2026 12:51:16 AM\r\nStarted autonomous agent loop for PRD completion\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Story: Create blog system with static TypeScript data\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts` — BlogPost interface + 6 full travel articles about JB\r\n- `site/src/components/BlogCard.tsx` — reusable card with category badge, excerpt, date, read time\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/page.tsx` — listing page with grid, metadata, OG tags\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` — article page with generateMetadata, prose content, tags, back link\r\n- Installed `@tailwindcss/typography` and added to tailwind.config.ts plugins\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Next.js `params` must be `Promise<{slug: string}>` and awaited in App Router (Next.js 15 async params)\r\n- No ESLint config present — skip lint, use tsc only\r\n- Pages import Header/Footer directly; no layout wrapping per route\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- `@tailwindcss/typography` was not installed — needed npm install + tailwind.config.ts plugin registration\r\n- `params` in App Router Next.js 15 is async (Promise), must `await params` before destructuring\r\n\r\n...\n</persisted-output>\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da0fa83d-ba02-4da7-93da-79913d071b9e","uuid":"da6eaf49-d63f-4162-9cfa-11edf704ed99","timestamp":"2026-04-13T18:38:27.989Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Codebase Patterns\r\n\r\n- Pages use `<Header />` + `<Footer />` from `@/components/`, wrapped in `<main className=\"min-h-screen bg-stone-50\">`\r\n- Content sections use `pt-28 pb-16 container-custom` for top-padding that clears the fixed header\r\n- `font-display` maps to Playfair Display (serif); `font-sans` maps to Inter\r\n- Tailwind custom colors: `stone-*`, `amber-*`, `primary-*`, `accent-*`, `sand-*`\r\n- Data files live in `site/src/data/` and export typed interfaces + arrays\r\n- Next.js App Router with `generateMetadata` for SEO; `metadataBase` set in layout.tsx\r\n- `@tailwindcss/typography` installed (iteration 1) — use `prose prose-stone prose-lg` for HTML content rendering\r\n- No ESLint config in project — skip `npm run lint`; use `npx tsc --noEmit` as the quality check\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Ralph Progress Log - Fri, Mar 13, 2026 12:51:16 AM\r\nStarted autonomous agent loop for PRD completion\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Story: Create blog system with static TypeScript data\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts` — BlogPost interface + 6 full travel articles about JB\r\n- `site/src/components/BlogCard.tsx` — reusable card with category badge, excerpt, date, read time\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/page.tsx` — listing page with grid, metadata, OG tags\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` — article page with generateMetadata, prose content, tags, back link\r\n- Installed `@tailwindcss/typography` and added to tailwind.config.ts plugins\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Next.js `params` must be `Promise<{slug: string}>` and awaited in App Router (Next.js 15 async params)\r\n- No ESLint config present — skip lint, use tsc only\r\n- Pages import Header/Footer directly; no layout wrapping per route\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- `@tailwindcss/typography` was not installed — needed npm install + tailwind.config.ts plugin registration\r\n- `params` in App Router Next.js 15 is async (Promise), must `await params` before destructuring\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026 12:58:18 AM\r\nCompleted: Create blog system with static TypeScript data (ID: US-001) in 6m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-002 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a Next.js/TypeScript project, not Frappe/Python. The implementation will be in a TypeScript data file.\r\n\r\nHere is the technical brief for the agent:\r\n\r\n**Objective:** Create 6 SEO-optimized blog articles for the Pelangi Capsule Hostel website.\r\n\r\n**File to Modify:**\r\n*   `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`: This is the main file. You will add 6 new post objects to the array exported from this file.\r\n\r\n**Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Define 6 new objects within the `posts` array in `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`.\r\n2.  Each object represents one article and must conform to the existing data structure (likely including `id`, `slug`, `title`, `date`, `category`, `tags`, `excerpt`, and `content`).\r\n3.  For each object, write original, high-quality article content (600-900 words) for the `content` field based on the 6 specified topics.\r\n4.  The content should be a string, likely using template literals to handle multi-line text and embedded HTML (e.g., `<p>`, `<a>` tags).\r\n5.  Embed 2-3 internal links (e.g., `<a href=\"/guide\">...</a>`) within the content of each article as specified.\r\n6.  Populate all metadata fields (slug, title, excerpt, etc.) for each post, ensuring slugs are unique and SEO-friendly.\r\n\r\n**Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\r\n*   **Content is King:** The core task is writing original, well-researched content. Do not copy-paste from sources.\r\n*   **Slugs:** Ensure all 6 slugs are unique to prevent page routing conflicts.\r\n*   **Internal Links:** Double-check that the link paths (`/guide`, `/rooms`, `/book`) are correct.\r\n*   **Data Consistency:** Match the format of existing entries in `posts.ts` for dates, categories, and tags.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:04:30 AM\r\nIncomplete: Write 6 SEO-optimised travel blog articles about JB for backpackers (ID: US-002) — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n## Iteration 3 - Thu, Mar 13, 2026\r\nCompleted: Write 6 SEO-optimised travel blog articles about JB for backpackers (ID: US-002) — attempt 2/3\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- All 6 articles were already present in posts.ts (created during US-001 implementation)\r\n- Verified all acceptance criteria pass:\r\n  - 6 unique slugs, titles, excerpts, categories, dates, tags\r\n  - Word counts: 676–831 (all within 600–900 range)\r\n  - Each article has 3 internal links (/guide, /rooms, /book)\r\n  - Topics covered: food, border crossing, budget activities, hawker centers, JB vs SG, hidden gems\r\n  - SEO-friendly titles with target keywords\r\n  - Categories: Food & Drink, Travel Tips, Things To Do, Local Life\r\n- TypeScript compiles without errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- US-001 iteration created both the blog system AND all 6 articles in one pass\r\n- Previous iteration likely failed to verify the articles were already there\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Always verify existing state before assuming work needs to be done\r\n\r\n## Iteration 3 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:09:04 AM\r\nCompleted: Write 6 SEO-optimised travel blog articles about JB for backpackers (ID: US-002) in 4m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-005 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nHere is the technical brief for user story US-005.\r\n\r\n**Subject: Technical Brief for US-005: SEO Structured Data Implementation**\r\n\r\nThis story requires adding JSON-LD structured data to a Next.js website. The project is TypeScript/React, not Frappe/Python.\r\n\r\n**1. Python Files to Modify (Next.js/TSX Equivalents):**\r\n*   `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`: To render `Article` and `BreadcrumbList` schemas.\r\n*   `site/src/app/blog/page.tsx`: To render `BreadcrumbList` schema on the blog index.\r\n*   `site/src/app/page.tsx`: To add `FAQPage` schema for the FAQ section.\r\n*   `site/src/components/BlogStructuredData.tsx`: A new component to create for generating the schemas.\r\n\r\n**2. Frappe DocTypes/Hooks Involved (Next.js Equivalents):**\r\n*   **Pages (Routes):** `/blog/[slug]`, `/blog`, and the homepage (`/`).\r\n*   **Components:** A new server component is needed to encapsulate schema generation logic.\r\n*   **Props:** The component will accept post data (headline, description, date, image) and the current page path.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Create a new component `site/src/components/BlogStructuredData.tsx`.\r\n2.  This component will accept props for post details and generate `BlogPosting` and `BreadcrumbList` JSON objects.\r\n3.  It will render a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag containing the stringified JSON.\r\n4.  Use this component in `[slug]/page.tsx` (for both schemas) and `blog/page.tsx` (for BreadcrumbList).\r\n5.  Create a similar, separate component for the `FAQPage` schema and use it on the homepage.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   All URLs in the schema (`@id`, `image`, `logo`) **must** be absolute, not relative.\r\n*   Ensure the post data object passed as props contains all required fields (e.g., `datePublished`, `image`).\r\n*   Validate the final output using the Google Rich Results Test, as JSON-LD syntax is strict.\r\n*   The publisher logo URL is provided in the technical notes.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration N - Story: Add Article schema and BreadcrumbList structured data to blog pages (US-005)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/components/BlogStructuredData.tsx` — new component accepting BlogPost prop\r\n  - Renders BlogPosting JSON-LD (headline, description, datePublished, author, publisher+logo, image, url, mainEntityOfPage)\r\n  - Renders BreadcrumbList JSON-LD: Home > Blog > Article Title\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` — imported BlogStructuredData, rendered before <Header>\r\n- `site/src/app/blog/page.tsx` — added inline BreadcrumbList JSON-LD (Home > Blog) as module-level const + script tag\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- JSON-LD script tags placed directly in JSX as children of <main> work fine in Next.js App Router\r\n- Existing StructuredData.tsx pattern: inline schema objects + dangerouslySetInnerHTML — followed same approach\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- blog/page.tsx is a Server Component (no \"use client\") but uses module-level const for schema — this is fine as it's static data\r\n- featuredImage paths may be relative (/images/...) — handled by prepending hostname if not absolute\r\n## Iteration 4 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:12:26 AM\r\nCompleted: Add Article schema and BreadcrumbList structured data to blog pages (ID: US-005) in 3m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration - Story: Update sitemap.ts to include all blog posts (US-006)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Imported `blogPosts` from `@/data/blog/posts` in `site/src/app/sitemap.ts`\r\n- Added `/blog` listing page entry with `priority: 0.8`, `changeFrequency: 'weekly'`\r\n- Dynamically mapped all blog posts to sitemap entries with `priority: 0.7`, `changeFrequency: 'monthly'`, using `new Date(post.date)` for `lastModified`\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Export name is `blogPosts` (not `posts`) — check actual export names before importing\r\n- `MetadataRoute.Sitemap` type annotation on the mapped array avoids TypeScript issues with spread\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- None — straightforward story\r\n## Iteration 5 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:15:09 AM\r\nCompleted: Update sitemap.ts to include all blog posts (ID: US-006) in 2m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 6 - Story: Add RSS/Atom feed at /feed.xml for the blog (US-003)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/app/feed.xml/route.ts` — Next.js Route Handler that:\r\n  - Imports blogPosts from @/data/blog/posts\r\n  - Sorts posts by date (newest first)\r\n  - Generates valid RSS 2.0 XML with proper namespaces\r\n  - Includes channel metadata (title, link, description, language, lastBuildDate)\r\n  - Maps each post to RSS <item> with: title, link, description (excerpt), pubDate, category, guid\r\n  - Uses CDATA for content field (safely embeds HTML)\r\n  - Escapes XML special characters (&, <, >, \", ')\r\n  - Returns Response with Content-Type: application/xml and cache headers\r\n- `site/src/app/layout.tsx` — added RSS feed link to metadata.alternates.types\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Next.js Route Handlers at /app/[route]/route.ts replace Express-style endpoints\r\n- RSS feeds should sort posts newest-first for feed reader UX\r\n- CDATA sections in RSS allow raw HTML content without escaping\r\n- metadata.alternates.types is the Next.js way to add alternate links (RSS, etc.) to layout metadata\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- XML special chars must be escaped in channel/item metadata but not in CDATA\r\n- RSS 2.0 uses RFC 822 date format (toUTCString())\r\n\r\n## Iteration 6 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:18:00 AM\r\nCompleted: Add RSS/Atom feed at /feed.xml for the blog (ID: US-003) in 3m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 6 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:18:20 AM\r\nIncomplete: Add 'Singapore Day Trip' teaser section to homepage (ID: US-008) — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration N - Story: Enhance /guide page with rich backpacker-focused local content (US-007)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Rewrote `site/src/app/guide/page.tsx` with 7 content sections:\r\n  1. Getting Around JB — GrabCar/taxi/bus fares with real prices\r\n  2. Money & Currency — Jalan Wong Ah Fook changers, ATMs, approximate rates table\r\n  3. Singapore Day Trip — Causeway vs Second Link, hours, bus numbers, immigration tip\r\n  4. Top Hawker Centres Near Us — 4 hawker spots with distance and hours\r\n  5. Restaurants Near Us (enhanced original section with opening hours)\r\n  6. Safety Tips for Backpackers — 4 categories\r\n  7. Useful Local Apps — Grab, MyRapid, Google Maps, XE Currency, MySejahtera\r\n- Added `generateMetadata` with 'Johor Bahru local guide backpacker' keywords\r\n- Added internal Links to /blog/singapore-to-jb-day-trip-causeway-guide and /blog/jb-hawker-centres-street-food-must-visit\r\n- Added quick-nav anchor links at top\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Quick-nav anchors work with section `id` attributes and `href=\"#id\"` anchors\r\n- `border-l-4 border-l-{color}` creates colored left border accent on cards\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- None — straightforward content + Tailwind work\r\n## Iteration 7 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:23:14 AM\r\nIncomplete: Add 'Singapore Day Trip' teaser section to homepage (ID: US-008) — attempt 2/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 8 - Story: Add JB News & Updates widget on homepage using curated RSS links (US-004)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/components/JBBuzz.tsx` — new component with two columns:\r\n  - Left (3/5): 5 curated news cards from Malay Mail, The Star, Visit Johor, Johor Now with title, source, date, description\r\n  - Right (2/5): 3 latest blog posts using existing BlogCard component\r\n  - RSS subscribe button linking to /feed.xml\r\n- `site/src/app/page.tsx` — imported JBBuzz, placed after CommunityEvents and before Teaser section\r\n- All external links use target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\r\n- Design matches stone/amber color scheme with rounded-2xl cards\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- BlogCard component is reusable — import and pass post data directly\r\n- Curated news is static data (no runtime API calls) — avoids SSR issues\r\n- Section ordering: CommunityEvents → JBBuzz → Teaser\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- None — straightforward component creation\r\n\r\n## Iteration 9 - Story: Add 'Singapore Day Trip' teaser section to homepage (US-008)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/components/SingaporeTeaser.tsx` — new component with:\r\n  - Gradient background: `from-amber-50 via-amber-100 to-amber-50` for eye-catching appearance\r\n  - 3 stat cards in responsive grid (md:grid-cols-3):\r\n    1. \"30 Minutes\" — distance to Marina Bay via Causeway\r\n    2. \"70% Less\" — cost savings vs Singapore accommodation\r\n    3. \"Flexible\" — day trip or stay longer option\r\n  - Each card has amber-100 bg, white body, rounded-2xl, shadow-lg with amber border\r\n  - SVG icons in circular amber backgrounds\r\n  - Two CTA buttons: \"Read Day Trip Guide\" (btn-primary) and \"View Local Guide\" (btn-secondary)\r\n  - Links to `/blog/singapore-to-jb-day-trip-causeway-guide` and `/guide`\r\n- `site/src/app/page.tsx` — imported SingaporeTeaser and placed between `<LocationMap />` and `<FAQ />`\r\n- `npm run build` passes with zero errors, all 21 pages generated successfully\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Gradient backgrounds (from-color via-color to-color) work well for section differentiation\r\n- SVG icons in circular containers (w-16 h-16 rounded-full) are consistent with site design\r\n- Two-button CTA pattern (primary + secondary) provides good call-to-action flexibility\r\n- Responsive grid with md:grid-cols-3 falls back to single column on mobile\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- None — straightforward component following existing site patterns\r\n\r\n## Iteration 9 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:35:00 AM\r\nCompleted: Add 'Singapore Day Trip' teaser section to homepage (ID: US-008) in 8m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 9 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:37:08 AM\r\nCompleted: Add 'Singapore Day Trip' teaser section to homepage (ID: US-008) in 8m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-009 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a **Next.js/React frontend**, not Frappe/Python. The implementation will be in TypeScript within the `site` directory.\r\n\r\n**Technical Brief for US-009:**\r\n\r\n1.  **Files to Modify:**\r\n    *   **Create:** `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`. This is a new page file as specified in the technical notes.\r\n    *   **Reference/Reuse:** Potentially `site/src/components/ui/button.tsx` for CTAs and other components in `site/src/components/` for layout and card elements to maintain consistency.\r\n\r\n2.  **Frappe DocTypes / Hooks:**\r\n    *   None. This is a Next.js frontend task. No Frappe or Python backend code is involved.\r\n\r\n3.  **Implementation Approach:**\r\n    *   Create a standard React Server Component at `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`.\r\n    *   Add a `generateMetadata` export to set the page title and description for SEO.\r\n    *   Build the UI using JSX and Tailwind CSS, following the existing site's stone/amber color scheme.\r\n    *   The primary CTA should be an `<a>` tag styled as a button, pointing to the pre-filled WhatsApp URL: `https://wa.me/60127088789?text=Hi%20Pelangi%20Capsule%20Hostel!%20I'd%20like%20to%20book%20a%20pod.%20Please%20confirm%20availability%20for%20[dates].`\r\n    *   Add sections for \"Direct Booking Benefits,\" \"Pricing,\" and \"House Rules.\"\r\n    *   Include secondary links for the property's Booking.com and Hostelworld pages.\r\n\r\n4.  **Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n    *   The Booking.com and Hostelworld URLs are not provided in the story and will need to be sourced.\r\n    *   The WhatsApp message template includes a `[dates]` placeholder; the button will simply open the link with the placeholder for the user to edit manually.\r\n    *   Ensure all elements are fully responsive and match the existing site's design language.\r\n    *   The story mentions `Booking.tsx`, which doesn't exist. The UI for OTA links should be built inline using existing component patterns.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 10 - Story: Create /book page with direct booking + OTA options (US-009)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `site/src/app/book/page.tsx` — full booking page with:\r\n  - Hero section with amber gradient and primary WhatsApp CTA (pre-filled message)\r\n  - Pricing section: nightly (RM35-45) and monthly (RM594) with comparison\r\n  - Direct booking benefits: 4 cards (no fees, instant confirm, pay at arrival, personal service)\r\n  - OTA platform links: Booking.com, Hostelworld, Agoda (from existing Booking.tsx data)\r\n  - House rules: check-in 2PM, check-out 12PM, no smoking, quiet hours, ID required, keep clean\r\n  - Contact CTA with WhatsApp and phone links\r\n  - Internal links to /rooms, /guide, /check-in\r\n- `generateMetadata` with SEO keywords targeting 'book capsule hostel JB'\r\n- Canonical URL set\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` both pass (22 pages generated)\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Existing `Booking.tsx` component has all OTA URLs — reuse data, not component (page needs different layout)\r\n- `_page.tsx.bak` existed from a previous attempt — the old version just wrapped `<Booking />`\r\n- PRD says check-in 2:00 PM but Rooms.tsx and Booking.tsx show 3:00 PM — used 2:00 PM per PRD business data\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- None — straightforward page creation following existing patterns\r\n\r\n## Iteration 10 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026\r\nCompleted: Create /book page with direct booking + OTA options (ID: US-009)\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:52:43 AM\r\nCompleted: Create /book page with direct booking + OTA options (ID: US-009) in 6m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-010 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a **Next.js** project, not Frappe/Python. The goal is to create a custom 404 page.\r\n\r\n### Technical Brief: Custom 404 Page (US-010)\r\n\r\n**1. Files to Modify:**\r\n*   Create a new file: `site/src/app/not-found.tsx`. This is the only file that needs to be created.\r\n\r\n**2. Framework/Components Involved:**\r\n*   **Next.js App Router:** This is a framework-level file. `not-found.tsx` is a special file convention in the App Router for handling \"Not Found\" errors.\r\n*   **`Header` & `Footer` Components:** Import these from `site/src/components/` to maintain consistent layout and navigation.\r\n*   **Tailwind CSS:** Use existing brand colors (amber, stone) and utility classes for styling.\r\n\r\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\r\n*   Create a standard React functional component in `site/src/app/not-found.tsx`.\r\n*   Wrap the page content in the existing `Header` and `Footer` components.\r\n*   Use a `main` element with a `div` inside, centered on the page (`mx-auto`, `flex`, `flex-col`, `items-center`, `justify-center`).\r\n*   Add a heading (e.g., `h1`) with the specified text: \"Looks like this pod is taken!\"\r\n*   Create a navigation section with `<Link>` components from `next/link` pointing to Home (`/`), Rooms (`/rooms`), Book (`/book`), Guide (`/guide`), and Blog (`/blog`).\r\n*   Include a prominent \"Book via WhatsApp\" button component or link.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   **File Naming:** The file *must* be named `not-found.tsx` and placed in the `src/app` directory. The older `pages/404.tsx` convention does not apply here.\r\n*   **HTTP Status:** Next.js automatically serves this page with a `404 Not Found` status code. No server-side logic is needed for this.\r\n*   **SEO:** Next.js also automatically prevents this page from being indexed by search engines. You do not need to add a `<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">` tag.\r\n*   **No Redirects:** Do not implement a programmatic redirect to the homepage. The purpose of this page is to handle the 404 gracefully, as per Google's recommendation.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 11 - Story: Create custom not-found.tsx (404 page) with hostel branding (US-010)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `site/src/app/not-found.tsx` — branded 404 page with:\r\n  - Large amber \"404\" heading + friendly \"Looks like this pod is taken!\" message\r\n  - WhatsApp booking CTA button (same pre-filled URL as /book page)\r\n  - Navigation pill links to Home, Rooms, /book, /guide, /blog\r\n  - Header and Footer for consistent layout\r\n  - Amber/stone color scheme matching site design\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- `not-found.tsx` in App Router automatically returns HTTP 404 status — no extra config needed\r\n- No `generateMetadata` needed — Next.js auto-sets noindex for 404 pages\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- prd.json must be read with `encoding='utf-8'` on Windows due to special characters in content\r\n\r\n## Iteration 11 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026\r\nCompleted: Create custom not-found.tsx (404 page) with hostel branding (ID: US-010)\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:56:00 AM\r\nCompleted: Create custom not-found.tsx (404 page) with hostel branding (ID: US-010) in 3m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-011 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nBased on the user story JSON, the request is for a frontend change in a TypeScript file, not a Frappe/Python backend task. Here is the technical brief for the specified work:\r\n\r\n**Project:** Pelangi Website (Next.js/TypeScript)\r\n**Objective:** Correct NAP (Name, Address, Phone) data in the site's structured data component to align with the Google Business Profile.\r\n\r\n**File to Modify:**\r\n*   `site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx`\r\n\r\n**Context:**\r\nThis is not a Frappe/Python task. The target file is a React component containing JSON-LD schema definitions for SEO. Two schemas, `hostelSchema` and `localBusinessSchema`, have incorrect, hardcoded values that need to be updated.\r\n\r\n**Implementation Plan:**\r\n1.  Locate the `hostelSchema` and `localBusinessSchema` constant definitions within `StructuredData.tsx`.\r\n2.  In both schemas, update the `telephone` property to `'+60127088789'`.\r\n3.  In the `address` object of both schemas, change `streetAddress` to `'26A Jalan Perang, Taman Pelangi'`.\r\n4.  Update the `geo` object's coordinates to `latitude: 1.48552` and `longitude: 103.75940`.\r\n5.  Set the `checkinTime` property to `'14:00'`.\r\n\r\n**Gotchas & Validation:**\r\n*   **Consistency is key:** Ensure the NAP data is identical across both `hostelSchema` and `localBusinessSchema`.\r\n*   **Data Formatting:** Geo-coordinates must have 5 decimal places of precision. The check-in time must be in `HH:MM` format.\r\n*   **Verification:** After deployment, validate the page URL with the Google Rich Results Test tool to confirm the structured data is correct and error-free.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration N - Story: Fix NAP inconsistency in StructuredData.tsx (wrong phone and address)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/components/StructuredData.tsx` — fixed both `hostelSchema` and `localBusinessSchema`:\r\n  - `telephone`: `+60123456789` → `+60127088789`\r\n  - `streetAddress`: `Jalan Maju, Taman Pelangi` → `26A Jalan Perang, Taman Pelangi`\r\n  - `geo.latitude`: `1.4855` → `1.48552` (5 decimal precision)\r\n  - `geo.longitude`: `103.7594` → `103.75940` (5 decimal precision)\r\n  - `checkinTime`: `15:00` → `14:00`\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Both `hostelSchema` and `localBusinessSchema` in same file share identical address/geo/phone — both must be updated\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- prd.json must be read/written as utf-8 on Windows (cp1252 default fails on em-dash characters in the file)\r\n## Iteration 3 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  1:59:09 AM\r\nCompleted: Fix NAP inconsistency in StructuredData.tsx (wrong phone and address) (ID: US-011) in 3m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-012 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nHere is the technical brief for user story US-012.\r\n\r\n**Project:** Pelangi Website (Next.js/React)\r\n**User Story:** US-012: Add FAQPage JSON-LD schema to FAQ component\r\n\r\n**1. Primary File for Modification:**\r\n*   `site/src/components/FAQ.tsx`: This is the most logical place to add the schema, as it encapsulates all the FAQ-related data and rendering logic.\r\n\r\n**2. Framework & Data Context:**\r\n*   **Component:** `FAQ.tsx` (React/TypeScript)\r\n*   **Framework:** Next.js (likely App Router, given `app/page.tsx`)\r\n*   **Data:** The implementation will use the existing array of question-and-answer objects that the `FAQ.tsx` component already maps over to render the visible FAQ list.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Inside the `FAQ.tsx` component, create a constant for the JSON-LD schema object.\r\n2.  This object's `mainEntity` property should be populated by mapping over your FAQ data array, transforming each Q&A item into a `{ \"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"...\", \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"...\" } }` object.\r\n3.  In the component's return statement (JSX), add a `<script>` tag.\r\n4.  Set the script's attributes: `type=\"application/ld+json\"`.\r\n5.  Inject the schema by using `dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: JSON.stringify(faqSchemaObject) }}`.\r\n\r\n**4. Validation & Key Considerations:**\r\n*   **Validation:** After implementation, copy the generated `<script>` content from the browser's \"View Page Source\" and validate it using the [Google Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results).\r\n*   **Content:** Per the story, ensure FAQ questions cover high-value topics (check-in, WiFi, price, location) and keep answers concise (1-3 sentences).\r\n*   **Safety:** `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` is safe here because you are stringifying your own trusted data object, not user-provided content.\r\n*   **TypeScript:** Ensure the new code is fully typed and introduces no TS errors.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration N - Story: Add FAQPage JSON-LD schema to FAQ component (US-012)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- `site/src/components/FAQ.tsx` — added FAQPage JSON-LD schema as `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` rendered via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\r\n- Expanded FAQ data from 5 to 8 items, adding: price (RM55/night), free WiFi, location (31 Jalan Trus), and Singapore proximity (15 min from Woodlands)\r\n- `faqSchema` const built from the `faqs` array using `.map()` so schema stays in sync with displayed content\r\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes with zero errors\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Client components (`'use client'`) can render JSON-LD `<script>` tags via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` — Next.js does not hoist these to `<head>` but Google can still parse them from the body\r\n- Wrap the component return in `<>...</>` Fragment to allow sibling `<script>` + `<section>` without a wrapping div\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- `prd.json` is UTF-8 encoded; Python `open()` must specify `encoding='utf-8'` on Windows (default is cp1252 which fails)\r\n## Iteration 4 - Fri, Mar 13, 2026  2:02:47 AM\r\nCompleted: Add FAQPage JSON-LD schema to FAQ component (ID: US-012) in 3m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-019 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nHere is the technical brief for the Next.js user story.\r\n\r\n**Subject: Technical Brief for US-019: Web App Manifest Implementation**\r\n\r\n**1. Files to Modify/Create:**\r\n*   **Create:** `site/src/app/manifest.ts` – This is the core file for defining the manifest.\r\n*   **Create:** `site/public/icons/icon-192x192.png` – A 192x192 pixel icon.\r\n*   **Create:** `site/public/icons/icon-512x512.png` – A 512x512 pixel icon.\r\n\r\n**2. Framework Hooks/Conventions:**\r\n*   This task uses a Next.js 15 App Router file-based metadata convention.\r\n*   The framework will automatically detect `site/src/app/manifest.ts` at build time and generate a `manifest.json` file served from the root.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  In `site/src/app/manifest.ts`, import `MetadataRoute` from `'next'`.\r\n2.  Export a default function `manifest(): MetadataRoute.Manifest`.\r\n3.  Return a JSON object from this function containing `name`, `short_name`, `start_url: '/'`, `display: 'standalone'`, `background_color: '#ffffff'`, `theme_color: '#a68b64'`.\r\n4.  Define the `icons` array with paths pointing to the new icons in the `/public` directory (e.g., `{ src: '/icons/icon-192x192.png', sizes: '192x192' }`).\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   Icon paths in the manifest must be absolute (e.g., `/icons/icon.png`), as they are relative to the public root.\r\n*   Browsers aggressively cache manifests. Testing changes may require clearing site data or using an incognito window.\r\n*   iOS does not support the automatic \"Add to Home Screen\" prompt; users must manually add it via the Share menu. This is expected behavior.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 5 - Story: Add dynamic OG images for blog posts using next/og ImageResponse (US-013)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `site/src/app/blog/[slug]/opengraph-image.tsx` — dynamic OG image generator using Next.js ImageResponse API\r\n- Exports size (1200x630), contentType ('image/png'), revalidate (3600s = 1h cache)\r\n- Generates unique image for each blog post with:\r\n  - Post title (large text, 56px, stone color)\r\n  - Category badge (amber background, white text)\r\n  - Formatted publication date and read time\r\n  - Site branding: \"🏝️ Pelangi Capsule Hostel\"\r\n  - Site URL and location footer\r\n  - Linear gradient background (amber light to white)\r\n- Uses generateStaticParams() to pre-render all 6 blog","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-Jyue-Documents-1-projects-Software-Projects-pelangi-website\\da0fa83d-ba02-4da7-93da-79913d071b9e\\tool-results\\bwhjllwmg.txt","persistedOutputSize":509959}}
